<!--
  GHS MULTI V850/RH850 64-bit arithmetic runtime call fixups.

  SINGLE AUTHORITATIVE SOURCE: V850CompilerHelperAnalyzer loads this file
  from the module data directory at runtime and installs any missing
  callfixup into the active program via SpecExtension (persisted with the
  program and honored by the decompiler). The compiler specs intentionally
  do NOT carry copies of these definitions; nothing is inserted from this
  file into any .cspec.

  ABI (GHS MULTI RH850, matching v850_ghs.cspec's __stdcall prototype):
    64-bit arg a in r6 (low word) : r7 (high word)
    64-bit arg b in r8 (low word) : r9 (high word)
    64-bit result  in r10 (low word) : r11 (high word)
    boolean result in r10 (0/1)
    shift count   in r8 (32-bit forms) or r8:r9 (64-bit forms)
  The join pieces are most-significant-first in Ghidra, so on this
  little-endian language the low word occupies the lower-numbered register.

  Signedness follows the GHS runtime contracts:
    div64/rem64/lt64/le64/abs64/shra_* are signed; udiv64/urem64/ult64/
    ule64/shrl_* are unsigned; add/sub/mul/and/or/xor/eq/ne/shll are
    sign-agnostic. The installed Hex-Rays V850 backend's helper descriptor
    table maps gh_mul64 and gh_mul64o to the same QWORD m_mul value lowering
    (table entries 0x3f5850/0x3f5868 in the recorded 9.5.261001 backend).
    This is a recovered decompiler value contract, not proof that the two
    physical runtime functions have identical overflow/flag side effects.
-->
